{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And every terumah.</b> The tradition has already established that the terumah mentioned in this passage is the firstfruits brought near to El, blessed be He — just as it is customary to bring firstfruits to the owner of the land, as it says: הִגַּדְתִּי הַיּוֹם לַה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ כִּי בָאתִי אֶל הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר נִשְׁבַּע ה׳ (Deuteronomy 26:3). And it states here that just as the restitution for the proselyte's stolen property, which belongs to HaShem, is given to the priest of the watch, so too the firstfruits brought near to El, blessed be He, are given to the priest of the watch."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:38:42.653716082Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}